<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>FITTEZ Refund &amp; Exchange</title>
  <!--
    The API key here is the Custom App's public API key (client id) --
    this is not a secret, it's the same value visible to anyone who
    inspects any embedded Shopify app's page source. The Admin API access
    token and API SECRET are never sent to the browser.
  -->
  <meta name="shopify-api-key" content="__SHOPIFY_API_KEY__" />
  <script src="https://cdn.shopify.com/shopifycloud/app-bridge.js"></script>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Inter, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 24px;
      color: #111;
    }
    #status {
      padding: 12px 16px;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      font-size: 14px;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
    }
    .ok { border-color: #1a7f37; color: #1a7f37; }
    .err { border-color: #c62828; color: #c62828; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>FITTEZ Refund &amp; Exchange — Admin</h1>
  <p>Auth wiring smoke test. This confirms App Bridge ID token verification
     is working end-to-end before the real dashboard UI is built.</p>
  <div id="status">Checking session…</div>

  <script src="/admin/static/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
